## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a comprehensive CAPA program with cross-tenant isolation, region awareness, and automation for policy drift scenarios during canary deployments. It probes API design skills, containment strategies, and the ability to define measurable impact metrics.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence linkage to logs and traces
- Region-aware lifecycle with staged gating
- Automated rollback and cross-tenant isolation checks
- Lightweight REST API for CAPA management
- Production metrics to prove recurrence reduction and effectiveness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express sketch for CAPA creation
app.post('/capas', async (req, res) => {
  const { tenant_id, policy_id, region, evidence_logs } = req.body;
  const capa = await capaService.create({
    tenant_id,
    policy_id,
    policy_version: await policyService.getCurrentVersion(policy_id),
    evidence_logs,
    region,
    detection_ts: new Date(),
    status: 'open'
  });

  if (capa.severity === 'critical') {
    await rollbackService.trigger(capa.policy_id);
  }

  res.status(201).json(capa);
});

// Automated rollback endpoint
app.post('/capas/:id/rollback', async (req, res) => {
  const capa = await capaService.get(req.params.id);
  const previousVersion = await policyService.getPreviousVersion(capa.policy_id);
  await policyService.rollback(capa.policy_id, previousVersion);
  await capaService.updateStatus(capa.id, 'containment_complete');
  res.json({ status: 'rollback_complete' });
});
```

